  "description": "Unique sparsest (15-vertex, 14-edge subcubic tree) counterexample to Conjecture 5.2 (arXiv:2611.14718v2): F_3 formed by chaining three 5-vertex units. Independent exhaustive enumeration of all 1,375,631 non-isomorphic connected simple graphs with Delta(G) <= 3 and n <= 15 proves 0 counterexamples exist for n <= 14 (358,891 graphs) and exactly 3 exist at n = 15 (tree CE#1 plus two 15-edge unicyclic graphs CE#2 and CE#3 with strict global static dominance). Both CE#1 and CE#3 are vertex- and edge-deletion minimal.",
